{"step_index":838,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-26T11:22:21Z","content":"Created At: 2026-10-26T11:22:21Z\nCompleted At: 2026-10-26T11:22:21Z\nShowing lines 1-89 of 89\n1: # Network Operations\n2: \n3: This is the authoritative documentation for the current network state.\n4: \n5: ## Settled Design (2026-10-19)\n6: **Architecture:** One two-way WARP tunnel (`wgcf-ingress`) from the decoy to the host.\n7: - **Tunnel Characteristics:**\n8:   - Decoy terminates WireGuard (`wg-opdbus`, 10.0.0.1).\n9:   - Decoy seals peer identity (OIA1).\n10:   - fwmark selects `wgcf-ingress` for egress.\n11:   - a simple plain TCP port (8090) is the target.\n12: - **Addressing:**\n13:   - Public host addressing: `pub0`.\n14:   - Internal fabric: `ovsbr0` retains OpenFlow `10.200.0.1`.\n15: - **Decoy Routing:**\n16:   - Administrative SSH (TCP 22/2222) is DNAT'd from `10.0.0.1` to `188.68.58.237:22` via table `ip wgcf_admin_ssh`.\n17: - **SOP:** No inner tunnels (GRE, SSH TUN, MASQUE, Xray) are required or active.\n18: \n19: ## Recovery evidence and deployment state (2026-10-20)\n20: - **Interfaces:** `ovsbr0` is UP and holds `10.0.0.2/32` (as an alias). `pub0` is the public uplink.\n21: - **Routing:** Local routing for `10.0.0.0/24` looks up table `28061`.\n22: - **Verified recovery:** `10.0.0.2:8090` listens and CA-verified HTTPS `/mcp` returns `401` for an unauthenticated request. Private listeners `127.0.0.1:1883`, `127.0.0.1:8085`, and `127.0.0.1:9000` are present.\n23: - **Verified MQTT path:** CA-verified `/mqtt` WebSocket upgrade through `10.0.0.2:8090` returns `101` with MQTT subprotocol. The private ExHook `https://127.0.0.1:9000/` responds `200` using the existing verified CA and client certificate.\n24: - **Release state:** Slot A has complete readiness; bridge and EMQX pass their real health checks using approved, backed-up maintenance overrides under `/var/lib/opdbus-release/maintenance-8090-20261020`. Corrected GNU bridge and opblob were built and a corrected golden filesystem prepared.\n25: - **Canonical deployment blocker (superseded 2026-10-20 ~22:44Z):** Reusing inactive root 450 had failed the exact-generation checked-delete with `EPERM` and the journal was stuck at `quiescent-delete:450`. **Resolved via the canonical path:** root 450 and source 449 were deleted by the release controller during `provision-slots` reconciliation, candidate 452 was installed into slot B, and the journal is now `None`. Slot A (root 315) remains the untouched active release; no activation or cutover has occurred. Pending: owner decision on replacing the now-stale 452/451 before any new deploy. See `/tmp/dashboard-decoy-e2e-20261020/recovery-probe/` for receipts. Still outstanding for a future activation: restore the canonical EMQX check stub, then remove maintenance run overrides after successful canonical cutover.\n26: \n27: ## Decoy HTTP forward and issuer origin (2026-10-20, `dashboard-decoy-e2e-20261020`)\n28: \n29: - **New forward:** decoy `op-main-web.socket` binds `10.0.0.1:8080` only (no `BindToDevice`, so private mesh arrival is allowed) and activates `op-main-web.service`, which runs `systemd-socket-proxyd 10.0.0.2:8080`. INPUT allows `-i wg-opdbus -d 10.0.0.1/32 tcp dport 8080` before the wg-opdbus REJECT, live and persisted in `/etc/iptables/rules.v4`.\n30: - **Verified:** `http://10.0.0.1:8080/` from the host returns 200 with bytes identical to direct `10.0.0.2:8080` (root page and a referenced static asset, sha256-matched); listener is bound to `10.0.0.1` only. Port `8090` is not forwarded; no public binding added.\n31: - **Issuer:** `op-decoy-issuer` drop-in `browser-auth.conf` `OP_DECOY_ISSUER_ALLOWED_ORIGINS` gained `http://10.0.0.1:8080` (existing entries preserved); only that service was restarted. The issuer still listens bound to `wg-opdbus` (`10.0.0.1%wg-opdbus:51888`), so the host's mesh route to `10.0.0.1` cannot reach it — the Origin allowlist change is config-verified only; end-to-end proof requires a real WireGuard client arrival.\n32: - **Boot ordering corrected:** `op-main-web.socket` originally had `Before=sockets.target` while also `After=wg-quick@wg-opdbus.service`, which ran after `basic.target` — a dependency cycle identical to the one the SSH socket already fixes. Added `op-main-web.socket.d/boot-order.conf` (`DefaultDependencies=no`, `Before`/`Conflicts=shutdown.target`, `WantedBy=multi-user.target`) and re-enabled so the socket is wanted by `multi-user.target`, not `sockets.target`. Cycle corrected by configuration; no reboot has been performed, so boot-time behavior is not proven.\n33: - **Frontend source:** `/srv/git/3tched.com` `src/grpc/door.ts` `PAGE_CONNECTOR_ORIGINS` gained `http://10.0.0.1:8080`. The pinned UI source and prebuilt assets are now prepared in-repo (`vendor/3tched-json-render-ui` and `target/ui-artifacts/3tched-json-render-ui`) but are **not published or deployed** — the live `10.0.0.2:8080` page still serves the prior build.\n34: \n35: ## Router standalone configuration reconciled (2026-10-21, `router-wg-match-20261021`)\n36: \n37: - Owner approved passwordless SSH inspection and backed-up correction on `root@10.0.0.9`. Live `wgdecoy` and persistent OpenWrt UCI already agreed: address `10.0.0.9/32`, endpoint `129.80.64.127:51821`, peer public key `3wRZU4Bebo78BXTBTdqQo/UJ54Hawe0iXN/BuHQ8G3k=`, AllowedIPs `10.0.0.0/24`, keepalive 25, MTU 1280. Recent authenticated handshakes and router-to-sled traffic establish this working path; the historical peer key in HANDOFF is not current.\n38: - Only `/etc/wireguard/router-decoy.conf` was stale. Regenerated it atomically from existing UCI settings, retaining the working router key without printing it. The formerly pasted standalone private key differs from the current UCI key. No key rotation, decoy change, UCI mutation, interface reload or service restart was performed.\n39: - Router-private backup: `/etc/wireguard/router-decoy-backup-20261021.OahMCo/{router-decoy.conf,network.uci}`. Directory mode 0700; replacement config mode 0600/root. The backup contains secrets and must remain private. Restoring the saved standalone file reverses this file-only change; do not activate it as a second tunnel.\n40: - Post-change evidence: exported private key derives the live router public key `4V4Wob4v8YxCcQ4nz95Jt3b/aQcAInLq+ABIvvS7/Qg=`; `uci export network` is byte-identical to the backup; `wg show` reports a handshake 74 seconds earlier; `ip route get 10.0.0.2` selects `wgdecoy`, source `10.0.0.9`; ping receives 3/3 replies; native wget of `http://10.0.0.2:8080/` exits 0. Authenticated application flow and router reboot were not exercised. No `oi` command exists on this router; native `ip` commands were used. `stat` is also absent, so permissions were verified using `ls -ld`.\n41: \n42: ## Panel-assisted auth diagnosis (2026-10-21, `panel-auth-20261021`)\n43: \n44: - **Confirmed failure boundary:** a fresh OIA1 obtained through the actual router `10.0.0.9` WireGuard path, forwarded unchanged by the existing UI `DoorClient`, reached the same-origin connector at `http://10.0.0.2:8080`. The first normal bootstrap read, `project.get_context` / `chat.context`, returned `UNAUTHENTICATED` with raw detail `Assigned%20browser%20identity%20unavailable`. The UI client's automatic `register_key` fallback was deliberately not invoked. This was the real UI transport executed on the main host, not a capture of the user's browser.\n45: - **Issuer works for that path:** router route selects `wgdecoy`, source `10.0.0.9`; issuer returns HTTP200, `Access-Control-Allow-Origin: http://10.0.0.2:8080`, and an OIA1 document with a credential present and advertised door `https://10.0.0.2:8090`. No assertion/SID1/private key was logged or persisted.\n46: - **Source explanation, not an inner-error receipt:** `crates/op-grpc-bridge/src/interceptor.rs:529-536` maps every `validate_bound_oracle` failure to this exact public error. Lines50-108 check the assigned stored session, authored SID1, SID1 validity, principal/session binding, peer revocation and credential commitment. `oracle_assertion.rs:68-91` selects the control-plane chatbot target. Shipped run-script defaults bind the current router public key to session `b0c777e3-0955-cd8b-3d01-ca12998cae28`, principal `1262e982-14c1-44d4-0771-7ce74213211b`. Running environment was not readable; do not promote shipped defaults to a verified runtime selector.\n47: - **Exact subcause unresolved:** current bridge logger is explicitly `svlog`/0700 at `/var/log/op-dbus/op-grpc-bridge-release`, denied to this `jeremy` session; no privilege bypass attempted. Mounted `plugins/identity_sled` returned EIO. The generic error alone does not establish that the record is absent rather than its credential rejected. Next action is an authorized, credential-redacted inspection of the assigned session/SID1 validation state, preserving existing identity and grants.\n48: - **Corrected deployment evidence:** live asset `/assets/immutable/chunks/CYD_vHRA.js` includes connector origins `.1`, `.2`, and `.4:8080`. This supersedes the earlier frontend-not-deployed statement for that specific change; it does not establish the entire release's activation state.\n49: - **Browser-vantage limit:** main-host Chromium shows the identity retry gate and `ERR_ADDRESS_UNREACHABLE` for the issuer, consistent with its WG-only socket. That is separate from the router-backed admission failure. User Chrome relay was unavailable, so no user-browser trace is claimed.\n50: - **Fusion used once:** exit0; Astra Pro and Qwen accepted, three other members failed with explicit insufficient-paid-credit HTTP404s. Panel recommended separating issuer/CORS from downstream identity admission; the checks above followed that distinction. Redacted prompt, panel output, completion and admission receipts: `/tmp/panel-auth-20261021.gMktXg/`. HEAD `051a20d056afba074e21d797aa34f8947c543c5a`. No application/auth/network/grant/service/deployment changes or test-suite run.\n51: \n52: ## Human identity and desktop RDP configuration (2026-10-22)\n53: \n54: - Owner explicitly chose restoring the existing human identity, not adopting the chatbot identity. OpenWrt `wgdecoy` now uses the saved human key, public key `0I5FNCuHAu62VctaNgOlJ7RgfejJpYe9Qd0VdPGesX8=`, alias `jeremy-wg-f036`, session `414fbc56-03fb-20ab-758a-bcc7a7cbdc0e`, principal `c9bdf32e-811d-2495-b688-277c9e5c4d36`. UCI and the live interface were updated. Decoy's old router peer was replaced with this key for `10.0.0.9/32` and persisted with `wg-quick save`.\n55: - Address `10.0.0.9/32`, endpoint `129.80.64.127:51821`, AllowedIPs `10.0.0.0/24`, and keepalive 25 remain unchanged. WireGuard still terminates on Decoy; none was installed on the VPS. The bridge's separate browser control-plane/chatbot binding was deliberately not changed to the human key.\n56: - Private rollback copies: router `/etc/config/network.before-human-identity-20261022T152114Z`; Decoy `/etc/wireguard/wg-opdbus.conf.before-human-identity-20261022T152114Z`. Keep these secret-bearing files private. No post-change handshake or authenticated browser reconnect was exercised.\n57: - Desktop Hypr-RDP 0.1.7 is configured in `/home/jeremy/.config/hypr-rdp/config.toml`, with PAM service `hypr-rdp` and listener `0.0.0.0:3389`. User unit `/home/jeremy/.config/systemd/user/hypr-rdp.service` is enabled for the graphical session and was started; service/listener and capture/input initialization were observed. This is a graphical-session service, not a claim that a usable desktop exists before login.\n58: - UFW admits TCP3389 from `10.0.0.0/24` only. OpenWrt's persistent `firewall.hypr_rdp_vpn` redirects WireGuard-zone traffic to `10.0.0.9:3389` to the desktop's wired `192.168.1.118:3389`, restricted to that source subnet, with no SNAT/reflection. Router firewall backup: `/etc/config/firewall.before-hypr-rdp-20261022T152351Z`.\n59: - Manual RDP check: from another WireGuard client use `10.0.0.9:33