gistered human session repair (2026-10-23, `door-session-repair-20261022`)\n70: \n71: - **Reproduced cause:** the real deployed UI obtained fresh OIA1 through the existing router WireGuard path and completed both bootstrap calls, then SID1 failed with `sealed identity has no matching provisioned container binding`. Mounted `identity_sled.get_own_identity` confirmed the existing human record intentionally has no native instance or Btrfs device. This is distinct from the old chatbot-assignment failure above.\n72: - **Repair:** `identity_session_binding_matches` in `crates/op-grpc-bridge/src/identity_sled_dispatch.rs` now applies the existing containerless-human rule to SID1 authentication, credential refresh and genesis-stamp validation. Any attached instance must still match exactly; service and unclassified identities cannot omit their instance. Registry/revocation, credential commitment, identity, transport, expiry and grants remain enforced. No identity, key, grant, container or storage membership was created or changed.\n73: - **Deployment:** one locked native GNU release build completed at 00:09:16Z; canonical `activate-golden.sh` completed at 00:15:07Z. The reviewed regression-only fixture correction followed the build and does not change production code. Durable build, activation and admission receipts: `/var/tmp/door-session-repair-20261022.q6JCuh/`. Before activation, both host FUSE views were refreshed normally, then `cf-mesh` restarted to release its retained old namespace; the old daemons exited naturally. No force/lazy unmount, daemon kill or container restart.\n74: - **Post-deploy UI evidence:** main-host Chromium running the deployed UI, with unchanged fresh issuer documents relayed in memory through the existing router WG interface, received HTTP200/CORS for the correct origin and three canonical CallMethod responses with gRPC status0. The credential rejection is gone. This is not a capture of the user's browser.\n75: - **Provider configuration restored:** the running bridge selected missing `/etc/op-dbus/model-providers.toml`; admitted read operation `b2a4f48b-95c4-4a17-87a9-ef7044062671` had unknown outcome. Mounted `tched_fs.get_receipt` was denied missing `cap.storage.3tchedfs.receipt.read@v1`; no alternate identity, database read or grant change bypassed that denial. Archive inspection found only a symlink to retired `/opt/op-dbus/current/etc/op-dbus/model-providers.toml`, not independent mutable settings. At 00:21:35Z the documented tracked `deploy/config/model-providers.toml` was installed only into the absent runtime path, root:root/0644, with identical SHA256 `a3d5a93ea3f5e092222900c00e2808967a1d31714826c137a16925164353f9e6`. Existing key references and disabled-provider settings were retained; no key contents or services changed. Rollback is removal of this newly created file only while it still matches that hash.\n76: - **Connected surface verified:** a fresh deployed-UI connection after restoring the prerequisite reaches `Connected`, shows the original human session's Personal namespace, loads the provider picker and reports `Ready`. This was a new bounded verification of the read path after repair, not an automatic replay of the unresolved operation. `connected-ui.json` and `connected-settings.webp` retain the evidence. No model was applied or inference submitted. Separate visible limits: Knowledge feed reconnects with socket code1006; `opencode_go` and `voyageai` refresh failures are reported with stored models retained. The browser navigation's network-idle wait timed out while the connected UI remained live; direct surface inspection and screenshot establish the connection result, not that timed-out wait. The owner-authorized targeted credential regression started only after deployment and remains pending.\n77: \n78: ## Current network — owner correction (2026-10-20)\n79: \n80: ONLY SERVICE INGRESS ENDPOINT: 10.0.0.2:8090. EMQX IS NOT ON 10.0.0.3.  \n81: ONLY SERVICE INGRESS ENDPOINT: 10.0.0.2:8090. EMQX IS NOT ON 10.0.0.3.  \n82: ONLY SERVICE INGRESS ENDPOINT: 10.0.0.2:8090. EMQX IS NOT ON 10.0.0.3.\n83: \n84: - Door, EMQX and Qdrant are reached through that one service ingress endpoint.\n85: - EMQX private backends remain on `127.0.0.1`: MQTT `1883`, management API `18083`, wake WSS `8085`. The existing bridge relays `wss://10.0.0.2:8090/mqtt` to the private WSS backend. Port `8084` remains owned by threetched.\n86: - The bridge's private ExHook backend is `https://127.0.0.1:9000`; retain TLS peer verification and the existing client certificate. MQTT CONNECT authentication and owner-topic authorization remain enforced.\n87: - `ovsbr0` retains OpenFlow `10.200.0.1`. No `10.0.0.3` broker alias is required or authorized by this correction.\n88: - Latest native deployment readiness, `2026-10-23T00:15:07Z`: `complete b release-67847196-f07a-4538-a4ba-4d2ec2a59938`, active root460/source459, previous A/root458/source457, no transaction in progress. Canonical activation completed with its built-in service readiness gates; bridge PID5494 executable SHA256 `c8937c7dee5f6b2f8e87ec060f1adf07ef9d693016448c0fe6179a6b8a25580b` matches the retained build. Live and persisted catalog manifests both hash to `0badd9cd84b7868f25ff04c1567996edd39ea214d195c94074d5c908cd2ab988`; the existing catalog was retained, not resealed. No reboot. Registered human credential admission, provider enumeration and the connected surface succeed in the router-backed deployed-UI check above; the user's own browser reconnect and actual model inference remain unverified.\n89: - This document is the sole location for network operational notes. Append future changes here, keeping the current network as the final section; do not duplicate network history, topology, status or notices in `SIGNALS.md` or `HANDOFF.md`."}
