Kit + Svelte 5 + Vite). Application interfaces must strictly use Svelte/SvelteKit + Vite + `@json-render/svelte`.\n  - Deployment invariant: No deployment script or hand-copying binaries. Deployment is Btrfs send/receive of the prepared golden filesystem snapshot into the inactive slot (`Slot A` / `Slot B`) via `./activate-golden.sh` (`op-release-launch release`), which swaps read-only overlays live without host reboot.\n  - Kernel guard (`op-storage-kernel-guard`): Prevents unauthorized creation of Btrfs subvolumes outside authorized release/provisioning lifecycle.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Progress\n- **Mandatory Skills**:\n  - All 28 mandatory skill files specified in `AGENTS.md` were read and preloaded completely into context (`grpc-expert`, `grpc-protocol-expert`, `json-render`, `ovs-db-analysis`, `kernel-fuse-diagnosis`, `fuse`, `btrfs`, `incus`, `rust-memory-optimization`, `memory-safety-patterns`, `requesting-code-review`, `receiving-code-review`, `quality-auditor`, `verification-before-completion`, `agent-self-evaluation`, `application-security`, `rust`, `rust-patterns`, `rust-testing`, `svelte`, `svelte-code-writer`, `web-design-guidelines`, `unified-memory`, `using-superpowers`, and associated reference files).\n- **Catalog Sealing & Persistence**:\n  - Executed `sudo THREETCHED_CAPTURE_BIN=$(pwd)/target/threetched-artifacts/tched-router/threetched THREETCHED_CAPTURE_MANIFEST=$(pwd)/target/threetched-artifacts/tched-router/manifest.json target/release/opblob seal-shm`.\n  - Executed `sudo target/release/opblob persist`, successfully persisting 72 plugin blobs (including `chat_response`, `chat_router`, `tched_fs`, and `threetched`) and manifest to `/var/lib/opdbus/plugin-blobs`.\n- **Golden Preparation Dry-Run**:\n  - Executed `sudo deploy/lib/golden/build-golden.sh --dry-run` (task-794), which completed with exit code 0 (`[ok] golden preparation complete`).\n- **Router (10.0.0.9) Inspection**:\n  - Connected to OpenWrt router at `root@10.0.0.9` via SSH without password.\n  - Inspected `wgdecoy`: interface address `10.0.0.9/32`, public key `0I5FNCuHAu62VctaNgOlJ7RgfejJpYe9Qd0VdPGesX8=`, endpoint `129.80.64.127:51821`, peer `3wRZU4Bebo78BXTBTdqQo/UJ54Hawe0iXN/BuHQ8G3k=`, allowed IPs `10.0.0.0/24`.\n  - Handshake is active (latest handshake ~1m41s ago, 43 GiB rx / 3.39 GiB tx).\n\n---\n\n### 3. Key Findings\n1. **Root Cause of UI Chat Error**:\n   - The browser connects to `http://10.0.0.2:8080/`, which `op-web` serves from `/usr/local/share/op-dbus/dashboard-release`.\n   - `/usr/local/share/op-dbus/dashboard-release` is an overlay mounted read-only from Slot A (`release-9b52e195-0253-4616-8a98-2b2f16d9defb`, built Oct 23).\n   - The asset `2.BIbFq2gr.js` on Slot A contained the old client-side route block:\n     ```javascript\n     if (!singleton && !confirmedRoute) {\n       return { message: { content: \"Apply an available catalog model with a confirmed native routing binding before sending a chat message.\" } };\n     }\n     ```\n   - In `/srv/git/3tched.com`, `door-chat-adapter.ts` was already refactored to use `submitAndAwaitCommittedReply` via `chat_response`, removing that client-side check. But because the release overlay had not been updated to a new slot with the new UI assets, the browser was running the old bundle.\n2. **Subscribed Rendering**:\n   - `FeedBoundCanvas.svelte` uses `providePluginFeeds` and `plugin-feeds.ts` to hydrate `/plugins` and `/pluginFeeds` from `client.subscribeState` over gRPC-Web and doorbell notifications over WebSocket MQTT.\n   - On the old Slot A bundle, subscribed rendering is not executed properly because of the outdated client wiring.\n3. **Router Keys vs Chatbot Binding**:\n   - Per `docs/src/operations/network.md` (lines 52-56), the owner explicitly chose the human key on `10.0.0.9` (`0I5FNCuHAu62VctaNgOlJ7RgfejJpYe9Qd0VdPGesX8=`, session `414fbc56-03fb-20ab-758a-bcc7a7cbdc0e`, principal `c9bdf32e-811d-2495-b688-277c9e5c4d36`).\n   - The bridge's separate browser control-plane/chatbot binding (`b0c777e3-0955-cd8b-3d01-ca12998cae28`, principal `1262e982-14c1-44d4-0771-7ce74213211b`) was deliberately NOT set on the router because human session repair (`door-session-repair-20261022`) explicitly mapped containerless human authentication for the human key.\n4. **Golden Build Blocker during Live Run**:\n   - `build-golden.sh` failed during execution of `prepare-execution-python.sh`:\n     `execution environment requires native Python 3.14, found 3.13` (exit code 78).\n   - This occurs in `deploy/runit/prepare-execution-python.sh` which checks the python version required by `deploy/config/execution-python-requirements.lock`.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Errors & Fixes\n- **Error 1: `opblob seal-shm` failed with `capture threetched schema before sealing: unsupported threetched manifest format`**.\n  - *Root Cause*: `chat_router_paths.rs` defaulted to `/usr/share/op-dbus/threetched-manifests/tched-router.json` on the active Slot A overlay, which was format `opdbus.threetched.v1`. The new plugin code required `opdbus.threetched.v2`.\n  - *Fix*: Set `THREETCHED_CAPTURE_BIN=$(pwd)/target/threetched-artifacts/tched-router/threetched` and `THREETCHED_CAPTURE_MANIFEST=$(pwd)/target/threetched-artifacts/tched-router/manifest.json`. `opblob seal-shm` and `opblob persist` succeeded.\n- **Error 2: `build-golden.sh --dry-run` failed with `sealed threetched capture provenance does not match the prepared release binary and manifest`**.\n  - *Root Cause*: The persisted `threetched` blob in `/var/lib/opdbus/plugin-blobs` had older SHA256 hashes from the v1 build.\n  - *Fix*: Re-sealed with candidate binary and manifest environment variables and persisted to `/var/lib/opdbus/plugin-blobs`. Dry run then passed completely.\n- **Error 3: `build-golden.sh` failed with `execution environment requires native Python 3.14, found 3.13` (exit code 78)**.\n  - *Root Cause*: `deploy/runit/prepare-execution-python.sh` checked `python3 --version` and failed because host Python is 3.13 whereas `execution-python` requires 3.14 (or python binary path needs to point to the 3.14 installation in `/opt/op-dbus/execution-python` or uv tool python).\n  - *Status*: Unresolved; must be resolved to allow `build-golden.sh` to populate `/opt/op-dbus/golden`.\n\n---\n\n### 5. Active Context\n- **Active Release Slot**: Slot A (`release-9b52e195-0253-4616-8a98-2b2f16d9defb`).\n- **Services Currently Running**:\n  - `op-grpc-bridge` (pid 9111) on `10.0.0.2:8090`\n  - `op-web` (pid 12053) on `10.0.0.2:8080`\n  - `tched-router` (pid 6750) on `127.0.0.1:8084`\n  - `emqx` (pid 9965)\n  - `op-storage-kernel-guard` (pid 2255)\n  - `omp-auth-broker` (pid 2265) on `127.0.0.1:8765`\n  - `omp-gateway` (pid 2429) on `0.0.0.0:4000`\n- **Router State (10.0.0.9)**:\n  - WireGuard interface `wgdecoy` is UP and connected to Decoy (`129.80.64.127:51821`). Public key `0I5FNCuHAu62VctaNgOlJ7RgfejJpYe9Qd0VdPGesX8=`. Handshake active.\n\n---\n\n### 6. Next Steps\n1. **Resolve Python 3.14 Prerequisite in `prepare-execution-python.sh`**:\n   - Inspect `deploy/runit/prepare-execution-python.sh`.\n   - Check where Python 3.14 is located on the host (e.g. `/opt/op-dbus/execution-python/bin/python3`, `~/.local/share/uv/python/`, etc.) or how `prepare-execution-python.sh` selects `PYTHON`.\n2. **Execute `build-golden.sh` and `./activate-golden.sh`**:\n   - Ensure `THREETCHED_CAPTURE_BIN` and `THREETCHED_CAPTURE_MANIFEST` are set during release execution if required.\n   - Run `sudo ./activate-golden.sh` to populate `/opt/op-dbus/golden`, create the read-only Btrfs snapshot, transfer via send/receive to Slot B, and atomically rotate the overlays.\n3. **Verify WireGuard Keys vs Chatbot**:\n   - Explain to the user the key status on `10.0.0.9`: The router is currently running the human key `0I5FNCuHAu62VctaNgOlJ7RgfejJpYe9Qd0VdPGesX8=` with active handshakes to the decoy. If the user wants to switch the router to the chatbot identity or retain the human identity, verify with their intent.\n4. **End-to-End Verification**:\n   - Check `sv status op-web op-grpc-bridge tched-router`.\n   - Verify `http://10.0.0.2:8080/` serves the new frontend bundle.\n   - Test chat submission with `qwen3.5-35b-a3b` and verify subscribed canvas rendering.\n\n---\n\n### 7. Commitments & Constraints\n- **Preserve System Boundaries**: Never use `systemctl` (runit `sv` only). Never hand-copy binaries onto live targets. Do not reboot the host.\n- **Stop Over-Confirmation**: The user explicitly instructed: \"stop with the over confirmation i already said yes 3 times\". Proceed directly with technical execution without repeated yes/no loops for approved operations.\n- **Frontend Stack**: Svelte/SvelteKit + Vite + `@json-render/svelte`.\n</summary>\n\n# Conversation Logs\nStart with the compact transcript; if a step has `truncated_fields`, read only that specific line in `transcript_full.jsonl`:\n- `<appDataDir>/brain/<conversation-id>/.system_generated/logs/transcript.jsonl`\n- `<appDataDir>/brain/<conversation-id>/.system_generated/logs/transcript_full.jsonl`"}
